node_modules/
dist/
# ...but app/dist is the shell's connect screen, which is source, not build
# output — `dist/` above would swallow the one page the app ships (§28.3).
!app/dist/

# The desktop shell's build output (§28.3). The app's source is in git; a
# gigabyte of compiled Rust is not.
app/src-tauri/target/
app/src-tauri/gen/
# The staged sidecar (§28.4): a pinned Node runtime plus a production
# node_modules, ~300MB of other people's artifacts assembled by
# app/stage-service.sh. Rebuilt from the lockfile, never committed.
app/src-tauri/service/
*.log
.env
coverage/
ws-drive.mjs
ws-activity.mjs

# Playwright MCP scratch (snapshots, console logs) when driving the UI by hand.
.playwright-mcp/

# Bundled OAuth client (the ldflags equivalent) — never in git.
google-client.json

# Internal working ledgers and agent bootstraps — the delivery plan, the
# out-of-spec decision log, the shipped-rough-edges list, and the upstream
# to-dos. They are the author's working notes, not part of the release.
plan.md
plan-v1.md
JUDGMENT.md
LIMITS.md
DEP_TODO.md
architect_agent.md
implementor_agent.md
